url":"https://api.github.com/users/aryansennthilkumarGT/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Adds a loaded battery-pack closure task: one arm compresses twelve independent terminal springs through a loose pressure plate while the other inserts a separate retaining cross-key. Full score requires the contacts and retained preload to remain correct after both grippers withdraw. The fixed setup starts with all twelve cells loaded.\n\nThe distinctive operation is transferring distributed contact preload from a free plate to a free key. Comparisons with the four-cell holder (#1303), spring-flange blind clamp (#1403), and spring-hinged M.2 drive latch (#692) are documented in NOVELTY.md using their implementations. The task includes numerical partial scoring, original primitive assets, fixed layout, safety/invalid-state guards and reproduction commands.\n\nValidation of evaluated executable revision `1e7df189c4cf7e86ad57a9cb37fe584a7adfc5f3`:\n\n- Native PhysX at 480 Hz, robot actions at 20 Hz: 12/12 mechanism cases and 4/4 robot-control cases passed.\n- Two independent measured-state robot experts: 1.0 each, 1,677 actions each.\n- A third expert from a fresh HTTPS checkout: 1.0, 1,677 actions.\n- Actual Dream-1 beta evaluation: 0.0 over 3,600 actions, within the declared 180-second simulated limit.\n- Official media `M-JC9CBE`: actual model video, full-score expert video and setup screenshot. H.264/yuv420p, full decode and visual checks passed.\n- Static checks and blind-review text checks passed. Published Python, scorer, scene, physics probes, assets and all controller phase data match the evaluated revision; publication changes update documentation, measured result metadata, media ID and an unused controller status annotation.\n\nMeasured records and source provenance are summarized in validation.json. The model's failure is reported as recorded; the full-score experts establish feasibility.\n","labels":[],"milestone":nul